  "submitted_text": "Step 1: Treat the two boys as a single unit since they must sit next to each other. This means we have 7 units to arrange (6 girls + 1 unit of 2 boys).\n\nStep 2: Calculate the number of ways to arrange these 7 units. This is given by \\(7!\\) (7 factorial\n\nStep 3: Within the unit of 2 boys, there are 2 ways to arrange the boys (either Boy A sits to the left of Boy B or Boy B sits to the left of Boy A).\n\nStep 4: Multiply the number of arrangements of the 7 units by the number of ways to arrange the boys within their unit. Therefore, the total number of arrangements is \\(7! \\times 2\\).\n\nFinal answer: \\boxed{10080}",
